method.description:
Alias for [method get_data] for semantic clarity. Returns a specific document from multi-document YAML results. Returns [code]null[/code] for error results or if the index is out of range. [codeblocks] [gdscript] # Parse a multi-document YAML string var yaml_string = """ # First document name: Alice --- # Second document name: Bob """
var result = YAML.parse(yaml_string) if !result.has_error(): # Same as using get_data() var doc1 = result.get_document(0) var doc2 = result.get_document(1)
print("Documents: %s and %s" % [doc1.name, doc2.name]) # Output: Documents: Alice and Bob [/gdscript] [/codeblocks]

Returns [code]true[/code] if the result contains an error.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# Parse a YAML string
var yaml_string = "key: value"
var result = YAML.parse(yaml_string)

if result.has_error():
    print("Error: " + result.get_error_message())
else:
    var data = result.get_data()
    print("Parsed data: " + str(data))
[/gdscript]
[/codeblocks]

Creates a success result with the specified data and optional style information.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# Create a success result
var data = {"key": "value", "list": [1, 2, 3]}
var result = YAMLResult.success(data)

print(result.has_error())  # Output: false
print(result.get_data())   # Output: {key:value, list:[1, 2, 3]}

# Create a success result with style
var style = YAMLStyle.new()
style.set_flow_style(YAMLStyle.FLOW_SINGLE)
var styled_result = YAMLResult.success(data, style)

print(styled_result.has_style())  # Output: true
[/gdscript]
[/codeblocks]
